{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 0, "result": {"protocolVersion": "2025-06-18", "capabilities": {"tools": {"listChanged": false}, "resources": {}, "prompts": {}}, "serverInfo": {"name": "ucas", "title": "ucas, a computer algebra system for programmers", "version": "1"}, "instructions": "ucas analyses functions (exhaustively on machine types), does exact algebra and calculus, transforms, number theory and finite fields, and finds cheaper implementations, each answer checked or proved.  Expressions are ucas syntax strings; give parameters types (x: u8, x: f32, x: real) where it matters.  Definitions persist across calls.  An ambiguous input is an error listing its readings: retry with args.assume.KEY.  structuredContent holds the typed result, checks and proof."}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "y^2 = x^3 + 2x + 3 over F_97\n  curve: y^2 = x^3 + 2x + 3 over F_97\n  discriminant: 62\n  j: 36\n  order: #E = 100\n  factored: 2^2 * 5^2\n  trace: -2\n  how: naive: 1 + sum over x of (1 + (x^3 + ax + b | p)), with a table of squares\n  check: (73, 83) has order 10 (N P = O, and (N/q) P != O stepwise for each prime q of N)\n  check: (46, 72) has order 25 (N P = O, and (N/q) P != O stepwise for each prime q of N)\n  check: N = 100 is the only multiple of 50 in the Hasse interval [79, 117]\n  supersingular: no (t != 0 mod p)\n  group: Z/50 x Z/2\n  check: P1 = (86, 28) has order n1; R = (55, 91); the Weil pairing e_n1(P1, R) = 96 has order n2, so <P1, R> has at least n1 n2 = #E points\n  twist order: 96\n  embedding degree: 4 (of r = 5: r | p^4 - 1)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 1, "ok": true, "cmd": "ec_info", "ucas": "ec y^2 = x^3 + 2x + 3 mod 97", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "ec", "curve": "y^2 = x^3 + 2x + 3 over F_97", "discriminant": "62", "j": "36", "order": "#E = 100", "factored": "2^2 * 5^2", "trace": "-2", "method": "naive: 1 + sum over x of (1 + (x^3 + ax + b | p)), with a table of squares", "supersingular": "no (t != 0 mod p)", "group": "Z/50 x Z/2", "twist_order": "96", "embedding_degree": "4 (of r = 5: r | p^4 - 1)", "lhs": "y^2", "over": "F_97", "value": "x^3 + 2x + 3", "headline": "y^2 = x^3 + 2x + 3 over F_97"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "(73, 83) has order 10 (N P = O, and (N/q) P != O stepwise for each prime q of N)"}, {"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "(46, 72) has order 25 (N P = O, and (N/q) P != O stepwise for each prime q of N)"}, {"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "N = 100 is the only multiple of 50 in the Hasse interval [79, 117]"}, {"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "P1 = (86, 28) has order n1; R = (55, 91); the Weil pairing e_n1(P1, R) = 96 has order n2, so <P1, R> has at least n1 n2 = #E points"}], "files": [], "text": "y^2 = x^3 + 2x + 3 over F_97\n  curve: y^2 = x^3 + 2x + 3 over F_97\n  discriminant: 62\n  j: 36\n  order: #E = 100\n  factored: 2^2 * 5^2\n  trace: -2\n  how: naive: 1 + sum over x of (1 + (x^3 + ax + b | p)), with a table of squares\n  check: (73, 83) has order 10 (N P = O, and (N/q) P != O stepwise for each prime q of N)\n  check: (46, 72) has order 25 (N P = O, and (N/q) P != O stepwise for each prime q of N)\n  check: N = 100 is the only multiple of 50 in the Hasse interval [79, 117]\n  supersingular: no (t != 0 mod p)\n  group: Z/50 x Z/2\n  check: P1 = (86, 28) has order n1; R = (55, 91); the Weil pairing e_n1(P1, R) = 96 has order n2, so <P1, R> has at least n1 n2 = #E points\n  twist order: 96\n  embedding degree: 4 (of r = 5: r | p^4 - 1)\n"}, "isError": false}}
